---
/**
 * The app's mark beside its name.
 *
 * ### Why this is markup rather than an image
 *
 * `art/wordmark.png` exists and is what the README uses, because a README cannot set
 * type. A page can. So the letters here are live text in Archivo — they inherit the
 * header's weight and tracking, resize with `clamp()`, stay selectable and searchable,
 * and never go soft on a high-density screen. Only the mark is drawn.
 *
 * ### The mark
 *
 * It is the launcher icon's: a node card with its output socket bulging out of the
 * right edge, lifted off the page by a darker extrusion. The geometry is the same
 * numbers as `art/icon.svg`, which `art/generate-icons.py` writes; if that script
 * changes the mark, this path data changes with it. The gradient and the highlight
 * the icon carries are left out on purpose — at header size they are one pixel of
 * noise, and a flat `--signal` is what the rest of the page is built on.
 *
 * ### The two things that make it belong to the word
 *
 * The card is `1.39ex` tall. That is not an approximation of the cap height — `ex` is
 * the font's own x-height, and Archivo's capitals run about 1.39 of it. Sizing off
 * the *font* rather than off a pixel value means the mark tracks the text through
 * every breakpoint on its own. The socket and the extrusion hang off that box, so the
 * SVG is a little wider and taller than the card and the viewBox says by how much.
 *
 * And `align-items: baseline` sits the card on the baseline with the letters, the
 * extrusion hanging just below it the way a descender would. Centring it — which is
 * what the placeholder square it replaced did — is what makes a mark look parked next
 * to a name instead of part of it.
 *
 * The gap is 0.22em: wider than a letter-space, narrower than a word-space, which is
 * the distance at which a mark reads as belonging to the name. `--track-tight` comes
 * off it because the letters are tracked and a flex gap is not.
 *
 * The label is on the anchor and the parts are hidden from assistive technology, so
 * this announces as "Easymatic" rather than as an image followed by a word.
 */
interface Props {
  /** Extra classes from the header or footer that owns this instance. */
  class?: string;
  href?: string;
}

const { class: extra, href = '/' } = Astro.props;
---

<a class:list={['wordmark', extra]} href={href} aria-label="Easymatic">
  <svg class="glyph" viewBox="100 126 316 272" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <path d="M170 138 H306 A62 62 0 0 1 368 200 V212 A56 56 0 1 1 368 324 V336 A62 62 0 0 1 306 398 H170 A62 62 0 0 1 108 336 V200 A62 62 0 0 1 170 138 Z" fill="var(--mark-shade)"></path>
    <path d="M162 126 H298 A62 62 0 0 1 360 188 V200 A56 56 0 1 1 360 312 V324 A62 62 0 0 1 298 386 H162 A62 62 0 0 1 100 324 V188 A62 62 0 0 1 162 126 Z" fill="var(--signal)"></path>
    <g fill="var(--mark-ink)">
      <rect x="160" y="184" width="126" height="34" rx="17"></rect>
      <rect x="160" y="239" width="90" height="34" rx="17"></rect>
      <rect x="160" y="294" width="126" height="34" rx="17"></rect>
      <circle cx="360" cy="256" r="30"></circle>
    </g>
    <circle cx="360" cy="256" r="16" fill="var(--mark-pin)"></circle>
  </svg><span aria-hidden="true">Easymatic</span>
</a>

<style>
  .wordmark {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    /* 0.22em is the optical gap; the tracking is subtracted because the letters
       beside it are tracked and the flex gap is not, so without it the mark would
       sit looser than the word. */
    gap: calc(0.22em + var(--track-tight));
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .glyph {
    /* 1.39ex is Archivo's cap height, and it is the *card's* height: the viewBox is
       272 tall of which the card is 260, and 316 wide of which the card is 260. Blocks,
       not inline, so the SVG carries no descender gap of its own under the baseline;
       the small negative margin drops the card's bottom edge onto the baseline and
       lets the 12-unit extrusion hang below it. */
    block-size: calc(1.39ex * 272 / 260);
    inline-size: calc(1.39ex * 316 / 260);
    margin-block-end: calc(-1.39ex * 12 / 260);
    display: block;
    flex: none;
  }
</style>
